text:
elaine: FYI CI publish failed for sample-sdk. prepublish hook bumped patch twice and npm refused the second publish (duplicate version). looks tied to typegen regen + auth retry. anyone seen this pattern?
ci-bot: [CI] publish:sdk failed 
ci-bot: changed files: package.json, src/types.ts
paul: can you paste the regen diff? want to ensure it's not a real schema change.
elaine: short excerpt:
```diff
-  "Item": {
-    "properties": {
-      "id": { "type": "string" },
-      "tags": { "type": "array", "items": {"type":"string"} }
-    }
-  }
+  "Item": {
+    "properties": {
+      "tags": { "type": "array", "items": {"type":"string"} },
+      "id": { "type": "string" }
+    }
+  }
```
ivy: ordering-only change again. typegen nondeterminism on object iteration.
paul: why did package.json get bumped twice?
elaine: reading CI logs: first publish run detected git diff and ran `npm version patch --no-git-tag-version`; that run hit a transient 401 on npm and auth-retry attempted to refresh token and re-run the publish step. the retry re-ran prepublish and bumped version again in the same workspace, producing x.y.(z+2). npm then rejected since x.y.(z+1) already published.
infra-bot: [infra] recommended: avoid mutating workspace during retry, or make prepublish idempotent and non-committing in CI.
ivy: agree. immediate fixes: (A) add spec canonicalizer to CI so regen is stable and avoids spurious diffs, (B) make prepublish bump ephemeral (in-memory) for the publish process rather than committing, or gate the bump behind a job that runs only once, not on retry.
paul: can we also change auth retry to not re-run lifecycle hooks? publisher should re-attempt network call only, not run npm scripts again.
elaine: I'll open a PR to: run tools/spec-canonicalize before typegen, and update CI publish job to skip git-commits on retries (use env CI_RETRY=true to short-circuit hooks).
ivy: add a typegen smoke test: regen locally and compare stable-signature hash (sorted keys + canonical enum order) against baseline. that will catch semantic drift vs ordering noise.
paul: long-term, consider vendoring a deterministic typegen binary in CI images so builds are reproducible.
ci-bot: [note] rerun requested by elaine 
elaine: thanks — will link PR and rollback steps when ready. keep this thread for follow-ups.
